# Definition of Done

> **Why this file exists:** a concrete, per-surface gate for what "done" means, so no
> agent claims completion without evidence. Satisfy the relevant surface(s) **before**
> committing or opening a PR.

## The rule
**Evidence before assertions.** Never say "done" / "fixed" / "tests pass" without running
the command and seeing the result. If a check was skipped, say so explicitly.

## How to run the gates
All gates run via the root [`Makefile`](../../Makefile) — one command, not loose commands:

| Surface | Command |
| --- | --- |
<!-- FILL: 1 dòng / app, khớp target trong Makefile. -->
| <<app>> | `make verify-<<app>>` |
| Everything | `make verify` |

## Universal (every task)
- [ ] Scoped to the requirement; no unrelated edits.
- [ ] Reused existing code; no needless new helper/component.
- [ ] Not in a gated/anti-goal area without human approval.
- [ ] Behavior change covered by a new/updated test (or skip justified).
- [ ] Docs updated if a contract/behavior/decision changed.
- [ ] Decision worth an [ADR](../adr/)? If yes, written.

## Per surface
<!-- FILL: 1 mục / app. Nêu check cụ thể (build/test/lint) + contract của app đó. -->
### <<app>>
- [ ] `make verify-<<app>>` passes.
- [ ] Response/contract shape unchanged (see [`../contracts/`](../contracts/README.md)); no breaking fields.
- [ ] <<app-specific check: layering, type-sync, a11y, no secrets logged…>>

## Before opening a PR
- [ ] Branch under `ai/`.
- [ ] PR body states what was verified and what was skipped — honestly.
- [ ] No merge / no push to `main`/`master` / no force-push.
